    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d915">

                <pb facs="0851" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1941v03/pg843"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/9748: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-04-09T18:00:00-05:00">April 9, 1941—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>39. Your 91, April 8, 5 p.m.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d915-f1"/> Reports recently
                    made public here state that the Yugoslav Minister in Ankara<anchor n="50a"
                        xml:id="d915-f2"/> has informed the <pb facs="0852" n="844" xml:id="pg844"/>
                    Turkish Government that Bulgarian troops have joined in the attack on
                    Yugoslavia, implying that Turkey is being called on to implement the Balkan
                    Entente. Please comment.</p>
                <p>The Department would appreciate being kept informed as fully and continuously as
                    possible regarding Turkey’s position vis-à-vis present developments in the
                    Balkans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
